          "text": "The pattern indexes as a body-centered cubic filled-skutterudite cell, with \\(a \\approx 8.884\\) \u00c5. The principal reflections are 200, 220, 310, 321, 400, 411/330, and 420. The composition and systematic absences select the LaFe\\(_4\\)P\\(_{12}\\)-type structure in \\(Im\\bar3\\) (No. 204). The Sb coordinates are estimated from the powder intensities and are less certain than the cell parameter.\n\n```cif\ndata_DyRu4Sb12\n_audit_creation_method                 'Indexed and solved from supplied Cu Kalpha1 powder pattern'\n_chemical_name_common                  'dysprosium ruthenium antimonide, filled skutterudite'\n_chemical_formula_sum                  'Dy Ru4 Sb12'\n_chemical_formula_structural           'DyRu4Sb12'\n_cell_formula_units_Z                   2\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type                 'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength           1.5406\n\n_space_group_crystal_system            cubic\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt              'I m -3'\n_space_group_name_Hall                 '-I 2 2 3'\n_space_group_IT_number                 204\n\n_cell_length_a                         8.884(2)\n_cell_length_b                         8.884(2)\n_cell_length_c                         8.884(2)\n_cell_angle_alpha                      90\n_cell_angle_beta                       90\n_cell_angle_gamma                      90\n_cell_volume                           701.2(5)\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_adp_type\n_atom_site_U_iso_or_equiv\nDy1  Dy   2  a  0.00000  0.00000  0.00000  1.0  Uiso  0.005\nRu1  Ru   8  c  0.25000  0.25000  0.25000  1.0  Uiso  0.005\nSb1  Sb  24  g  0.00000  0.341(5) 0.157(5) 1.0  Uiso  0.006\n```\n\nInterchanging the two free Sb coordinates corresponds to a powder-indistinguishable cubic orientation convention rather than a distinct structural alternative. No competing non-skutterudite solution is supported by the peak positions and stoichiometry.",
